
Java EXAM

1. Use TAP2/functional code (Gender, Person).
    a) The first goal is to create a select method that accepts
    a list of Person, a Predicate<Person> and a Query enum type (ALL, MAX). This static method will return
    a List<Person) with the Persons satisfying the query, For example:  SELECT * FROM PERSONS WHERE AGE>3, or
    SELECT MAX FROM PERSONS WHERE AGE>3. You can also pass as parameter a Comparator<Person>.
    Demonstrate in the code the use of closures.
    b)  The second goal is to make select method generic so that accepts List<T> and Predicate<T>,

2. Use TAP3/filesystem2 entire directory.
   a) Add to directory a search(Predicate<File)) method enabling queries using closures.
   b) Create a Decorator of Predicate<T> that counts the number of executions of the test method. Provide
   a getCountTest method returning an int with that counter.  Execute that decorator with a query (closure) invoking the
   search method in the previous section (a). Show that the counter correctly computes the number of
   times that test method was invoked.

 3. You can use TAP4/anotations and TAP3/filesystem2
    Create a new annotation called BlackList including a list of names.
    Use this annotation in the Directory class and include names of directories that must be excluded from the search.
    Check that when you search in a directory, all files inside blacklist directories are not processed,


